<title>COLOMBIA: Colombia clamps 15 pct tariff on imported wood.</title>
<headline>Colombia clamps 15 pct tariff on imported wood.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombia clamped a 15 percent tariff on wood imports from Venezuela, Ecuador and Bolivia as a barrier against unfair trading practices, Commerce Ministry said.</p>
<p>It said the measure, effective immediately, was adopted after a study by the Foreign Trade Institute determined that wood imports from the neighboring countries were cheaper than their domestic equivalents and causing a buildup of inventories that was hurting Colombia's lumber industry.</p>
<p>--Juan Guillermo Londono, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944</p>
</text>
